    "title": "Co-authors to discuss food from Revolution",
    "text": "There will be a presentation from the authors of “America’s Founding Food: The Story of New England Cooking” at 4 p.m. Wednesday, May 6, at the Jamestown Philomenian Library, 26 North Road.\nThe free presentation by Keith Stavely and Kathleen Fitzgerald will chronicle the food eaten during the American Revolution. The event is part of the semiquincentennial programming sponsored by the Jamestown Historical Society.\nReservations are encouraged due to limited capacity. Members of the JHS will be given priority.",
